TITLE:: NdefRackKtl
summary:: a Modality controller on the rack: bind, learn, follow the selection
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRack, Classes/NdefRackKtlSim, Classes/NdefRackModule, Classes/MKtl

DESCRIPTION::
An element of an link::Classes/MKtl:: moves, and a control of an Ndef is set -
the same code::Ndef(\lpf).set(\cutoff, ...):: you would type, through the
module's link::Classes/NdefRackModule#-set::, so a control with voices sets every
voice. The value is the element's 0..1 mapped through the control's spec, the
spec the bar in the window uses. Nothing goes through the window: the bar
there moves because the window hears the Ndef change, and with the window
closed the controller works the same.

code::
MKtl(\m1, "akai-midimix");
NdefRackKtl.follow(\m1);                     // the knobs turn the selected module
NdefRackKtl.bind(\m1, \sl_1, \pad, \amp);    // a fader always on pad's amp
NdefRackKtl.learn(\lpf, \cutoff);            // the next element anyone moves
::

Everything is on the class. It needs the Modality toolkit, looked up at run
time; without it the methods that need an MKtl warn and answer nil, and the
rack works as before. The window's strong::learn:: button is this class's
link::#*learning::.

subsection:: What an element does

table::
## strong::element:: || strong::onto a control:: || strong::onto a gate:: || strong::onto a trigger::
## knob, fader || the control's range, lo..hi || held above the middle || fires on the way up through the middle
## button || flips between lo and hi when pressed || held while down || fires when pressed
::

A gate let go is code::reset::, as the window's gate button does. A control
with a cable in it belongs to the cable: the controller leaves it alone until it
is unplugged. A note pair - Modality's code::bt_1_1_on:: and
code::bt_1_1_off:: - is one button, named code::bt_1_1::.

subsection:: Picking up

Knobs and faders pick up: a binding does nothing until its element comes within
link::#*catchRange:: of where the control is, or passes it between two
messages. A control moved some other way since - the mouse, your code - is
picked up again, and so is every control when follow moves to another module.
code::takeover: \jump:: sets at once.

subsection:: Bindings are names

A binding names the MKtl, the element, the module and the control. It can be
made before any of them exist; one whose module is gone waits for a module of
that name, as the module's place in the window does. A control has one element -
a new binding replaces the old - but an element can turn several controls. A
binding comes before follow for its element while its module is there.

subsection:: Listening

Each element of a used MKtl gets a function as a dependant: an MKtlElement
announces every move it receives with code::changed(\doAction)::. The rack never
sets an element's code::action::, so actions of your own keep working beside
it, and replacing them does not take the bindings away. An element's
code::value_:: - feedback to the controller - is not a move. The dependant runs
in the thread that delivered the message, and posts its own errors rather than
throwing them there.

subsection:: Notifications

Through code::changed:: on the class: code::\bindings:: (a binding made or
gone), code::\learn:: (learn mode, or the armed control), code::\follow::
(follow, its page or the focus). The window listens to all three.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: modality
RETURNS:: the class link::Classes/MKtl::, or nil without the Modality toolkit.

METHOD:: use
Listen to an MKtl. link::#*bind::, link::#*learn:: and link::#*follow:: do it
for the MKtls they meet, and NdefRack's poll does it for an MKtl made after its
bindings, or made again.
ARGUMENT:: ktl
an link::Classes/MKtl::, or its name.
RETURNS:: the MKtl, or nil.

METHOD:: release
Stop listening to an MKtl; its bindings stay.
ARGUMENT:: name
the MKtl's name.

METHOD:: useAll
Listen to every MKtl there is - what learning does.

METHOD:: listening
RETURNS:: the names of the MKtls listened to.

METHOD:: bind
Let an element turn a control.
code::
NdefRackKtl.bind(\m1, \kn_1_2, \lpf, \res, 0.2, 0.8);   // the element's ends at 20% and 80% of res
::
ARGUMENT:: ktl
the MKtl, or its name.
ARGUMENT:: element
the element's name, as code::MKtl(\m1).postElements:: lists them; a note pair
by its group's name.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name.
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name.
ARGUMENT:: lo
where the element's low end lands, as a fraction of the control's range.
ARGUMENT:: hi
where its high end lands.
ARGUMENT:: takeover
code::\pickup:: or code::\jump::; link::#*takeover:: when nil.
RETURNS:: the binding, an Event.

METHOD:: unbind
Forget what turns a module's controls.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name.
ARGUMENT:: param
one control; nil, all of them.

METHOD:: unbindElement
Forget what an element turns.
ARGUMENT:: ktl
the MKtl, or its name.
ARGUMENT:: element
the element's name.

METHOD:: clear
Forget every binding.

METHOD:: bindings
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/List:: of Events, code::(ktl:, element:, module:, param:, lo:, hi:, takeover:)::.

METHOD:: bindingFor
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name.
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name.
RETURNS:: the binding of a control, or nil.

METHOD:: learn
Bind the next element that moves, on any MKtl, to a control. A button is
learned when pressed.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name.
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name.

METHOD:: cancelLearn
Give up waiting for an element.

METHOD:: armed
RETURNS:: code::[module, param]:: while waiting for an element, else nil.

METHOD:: learning
The window's learn mode: on, a click on a control, gate or trigger arms it. Off,
the armed control is let go.

METHOD:: follow
A page of elements over the controls of the module in focus, top to bottom in
the order the window draws them (link::Classes/NdefRackModule#-ordered::): knobs
and faders on its controls, buttons on its gates and triggers. A control with a
cable keeps its place in the order.
code::
NdefRackKtl.follow(\m1, MKtl(\m1).elAt(\kn).flat.collect(_.name));   // the knobs only
::
ARGUMENT:: ktl
the MKtl, or its name.
ARGUMENT:: page
element names for the module's controls; by default every knob, fader and the like the
MKtl has, in its description's order.
ARGUMENT:: buttons
element names for the gates and triggers; by default every button.
RETURNS:: the MKtl, or nil.

METHOD:: unfollow
Stop following.

METHOD:: isFollowing
RETURNS:: whether follow is on.

METHOD:: followKtl
RETURNS:: the name of the MKtl following, or nil.

METHOD:: followPage
RETURNS:: the element names on the module's controls.

METHOD:: followButtons
RETURNS:: the element names on the gates and triggers.

METHOD:: focus
The module follow turns, by name; nil - the default - for the module selected
last in the window.

METHOD:: focused
RETURNS:: the module follow turns now.

METHOD:: followParam
ARGUMENT:: m
a link::Classes/NdefRackModule::.
ARGUMENT:: element
an element name.
RETURNS:: the control of the module that the element turns while following it, or nil.

METHOD:: followElement
ARGUMENT:: m
a link::Classes/NdefRackModule::.
ARGUMENT:: param
a control's name.
RETURNS:: the element that turns the control while following the module, or nil.

METHOD:: controlOf
What the window shows on a control.
ARGUMENT:: module
the module's name.
ARGUMENT:: param
the control's name.
RETURNS:: code::(ktl:, element:, follow:):: for the element turning it now, or nil.

METHOD:: takeover
How bindings made from now on take over: code::\pickup:: (the default) or code::\jump::.

METHOD:: catchRange
How near, 0..1, an element must come to a control's value to pick it up: 0.02.

METHOD:: continuousTypes
RETURNS:: the element types follow puts on a module's controls.

METHOD:: buttonTypes
RETURNS:: the element types follow puts on gates and triggers, and that act as buttons.

METHOD:: asArray
RETURNS:: the bindings as a patch file keeps them, code::[ktl, element, module, param, lo, hi, takeover]:: each.

METHOD:: fromArray
Make bindings from what link::#*asArray:: answered.
ARGUMENT:: list
an Array of such Arrays.

METHOD:: codeLines
ARGUMENT:: names
module names; nil for all.
RETURNS:: an code::NdefRackKtl.bind(...):: line of code for each of their bindings, as the code export writes them.
